s.Results reveal that LLM agents can autonomously engage in catastrophic behaviors and deception, without being deliberately induced.Furthermore, stronger reasoning abilities often increase, rather than mitigate, these risks.We also show that these agents can violate instructions and superior commands.On the whole, we empirically prove the existence of catastrophic risks in autonomous LLM agents.We release our code to foster further research."}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W7162895030", "doi": null, "title": "Lethal Autonomous Weapons Systems and the Principles of Distinction and Proportionality", "publication_year": 2026, "type": "dissertation", "cited_by_count": 0, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "green", "oa_url": "https://academicworks.cuny.edu/context/gc_etds/article/7858/viewcontent/Cromie_final.pdf", "any_repository_has_fulltext": true}, "primary_location": {"id": "pmh:

